{"Denial cache key omits authorization inputs like identity type/action sets and folder-tree context, causing a denial for one permission variant to be incorrectly reused for another request with the same namespace/user/action/name/folder tuple": 0.2628104090690613, "In-proc authz client now uses NoopCache which disables all client-side caching, not just authLib cache reuse as described in PR - this removes all client-side caching for in-proc client causing every request to re-hit the server": 0.6816555857658386, "In-proc and remote authz clients now have inconsistent caching behavior - remote clients retain client-side authz caching via cache.NewLocalCache while in-proc clients use NoopCache, causing divergent authorization semantics across deployment modes": 0.510239839553833, "Denial-cache tests only verify exact key matches but don't test key-composition edge cases like resources with same name under different parents, or same name with empty vs non-empty parent - the raw string concatenation key format without proper separators could cause collisions or false misses": 0.28858375549316406}